WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.519
(gentle music)

00:00:00.519 --> 00:00:07.788
Whether you're setting up a sponsored products campaign or wanting to optimize your existing ads,

00:00:07.788 --> 00:00:13.500
Amazon Ads creates recommendations that can help improve your campaign performance.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.107
These recommendations focus on targeting, bidding, and budget strategies, which help set up your

00:00:19.107 --> 00:00:20.180
campaigns for success.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.785
Targeting recommendations help show your ads to shoppers based on the keywords or products they

00:00:25.785 --> 00:00:27.340
are searching for on Amazon.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:33.095
Bidding recommendations include a bid amount that can help increase impressions and engagement for

00:00:33.095 --> 00:00:33.820
your campaigns.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.259
After reviewing your targeting and bidding settings, it's important to consider budget recommendations,

00:00:39.259 --> 00:00:42.360
which help your ads stay active and in budget.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.942
Now, you're ready to start optimizing your campaigns.

00:00:45.942 --> 00:00:47.780
Here's how to get started.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:54.387
Within the Campaign Manager, visit the targeting and budget pages to review past results for all

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:54.740
campaigns.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:01.212
If you find a specific campaign that you want to adjust, you can go to the Ad Group level to apply

00:01:01.212 --> 00:01:01.800
the recommendation.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.240
You may also occasionally receive recommendations via email.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.917
After making any adjustments, it's important to monitor your return on ad spend,

00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:13.800
ROAS, to track campaign performance.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.032
If you have questions as you're making optimizations and reviewing your results,

00:01:19.032 --> 00:01:21.500
visit the Support Center for more information.
